QQQ where is user = each.value.name is coming from? 
is it coming from here  4    name     = each.value1:00 PMYes, exactly! 🎯
hclresource "aws_iam_user" "dev_users" {
  for_each = var.usernames
  name     = each.value        # ← you SET .name here
}
hclresource "aws_iam_user_policy" "dev_users_policy" {
  for_each = aws_iam_user.dev_users
  user     = each.value.name   # ← you READ .name here
}
```

---

The flow is:
```
var.usernames = ["santosh", "nanda", ...]
       ↓
for_each = var.usernames
       ↓
name = each.value  →  sets .name = "santosh" on the resource object
       ↓
later... each.value.name  →  reads that same "santosh" back
So yes — .name on the policy side is reading the exact value you assigned with name = each.value on the user side. The resource object "remembers" all its attributes, and .name is one of them.
